{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-8075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Write the complex number $z=1+2\\text{i}$ in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/state.json" "file_sha256" "276dc118be4a2f41e3b3158f6df47dc739e8ff62c6b2beab881ba3abbadce57d"} {"question" "q-8075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To write $z$ in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the first quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2}{1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2) \\\\  & ≈1.107.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\theta =1.107$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.107\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/state.json" "file_sha256" "276dc118be4a2f41e3b3158f6df47dc739e8ff62c6b2beab881ba3abbadce57d"} {"question" "q-8075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b79df5d8e5d16fb4a9e8dca5d5f06b09d67e2cdebc7a13e7049f602b56100f29"} {"question" "q-8075" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/state.json" "file_sha256" "276dc118be4a2f41e3b3158f6df47dc739e8ff62c6b2beab881ba3abbadce57d"} {"question" "q-8075" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "z=\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{0.456\\,\\text{i}}"] ["math" "z=\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}"] ["math" "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{0.817\\,\\text{i}}"] ["math" "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.107\\,\\text{i}}"] ["math" "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/state.json" "file_sha256" "276dc118be4a2f41e3b3158f6df47dc739e8ff62c6b2beab881ba3abbadce57d"} {"question" "q-8075" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.107\\,\\text{i}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/state.json" "file_sha256" "276dc118be4a2f41e3b3158f6df47dc739e8ff62c6b2beab881ba3abbadce57d"} {"question" "q-8078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Write the complex number $z=3\\sqrt{3}+3\\text{i}$ in exponential form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/state.json" "file_sha256" "276dc118be4a2f41e3b3158f6df47dc739e8ff62c6b2beab881ba3abbadce57d"} {"question" "q-8078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To write $z$ in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3\\sqrt{3})^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36}=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the first quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3}{3\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=6$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=6\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/6}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/state.json" "file_sha256" "276dc118be4a2f41e3b3158f6df47dc739e8ff62c6b2beab881ba3abbadce57d"} {"question" "q-8078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b79df5d8e5d16fb4a9e8dca5d5f06b09d67e2cdebc7a13e7049f602b56100f29"} {"question" "q-8078" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/state.json" "file_sha256" "276dc118be4a2f41e3b3158f6df47dc739e8ff62c6b2beab881ba3abbadce57d"} {"question" "q-8078" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "z=4\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}"] ["math" "z=4\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/6}"] ["math" "z=6\\,{\\text{e}}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/3}"] ["math" "z=6\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}"] ["math" "z=6\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/state.json" "file_sha256" "276dc118be4a2f41e3b3158f6df47dc739e8ff62c6b2beab881ba3abbadce57d"} {"question" "q-8078" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "z=6\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/6}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/state.json" "file_sha256" "276dc118be4a2f41e3b3158f6df47dc739e8ff62c6b2beab881ba3abbadce57d"} {"question" "q-17516" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/assets/f13d134b7dba012b5b71a7a81ab8071b2706586699b8bf21a6df0d5c44c69619.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/state.json" "file_sha256" "276dc118be4a2f41e3b3158f6df47dc739e8ff62c6b2beab881ba3abbadce57d"} {"question" "q-17516" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x+\\text{i}y \\\\  & =3-\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{1}{3})| \\\\  & ≈5.961.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{10}$ and $\\theta =5.961$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get \n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.961\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/state.json" "file_sha256" "276dc118be4a2f41e3b3158f6df47dc739e8ff62c6b2beab881ba3abbadce57d"} {"question" "q-17516" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b79df5d8e5d16fb4a9e8dca5d5f06b09d67e2cdebc7a13e7049f602b56100f29"} {"question" "q-17516" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/state.json" "file_sha256" "276dc118be4a2f41e3b3158f6df47dc739e8ff62c6b2beab881ba3abbadce57d"} {"question" "q-17516" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "z=10\\,{\\text{e}}^{4.942\\,\\text{i}}"] ["math" "z=10\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.961\\,\\text{i}}"] ["math" "z=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/3}"] ["math" "z=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{4.942\\,\\text{i}}"] ["math" "z=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.961\\,\\text{i}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/state.json" "file_sha256" "276dc118be4a2f41e3b3158f6df47dc739e8ff62c6b2beab881ba3abbadce57d"} {"question" "q-17516" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "z=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.961\\,\\text{i}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/state.json" "file_sha256" "276dc118be4a2f41e3b3158f6df47dc739e8ff62c6b2beab881ba3abbadce57d"} {"question" "q-17518" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Write the complex number $z=-1+2\\text{i}$ in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/state.json" "file_sha256" "276dc118be4a2f41e3b3158f6df47dc739e8ff62c6b2beab881ba3abbadce57d"} {"question" "q-17518" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To write our complex number in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the second quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2}{-1})| \\\\  & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-2)| \\\\  & ≈2.034.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\theta =2.034$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2.034\\,\\text{i}}\\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/state.json" "file_sha256" "276dc118be4a2f41e3b3158f6df47dc739e8ff62c6b2beab881ba3abbadce57d"} {"question" "q-17518" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b79df5d8e5d16fb4a9e8dca5d5f06b09d67e2cdebc7a13e7049f602b56100f29"} {"question" "q-17518" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/state.json" "file_sha256" "276dc118be4a2f41e3b3158f6df47dc739e8ff62c6b2beab881ba3abbadce57d"} {"question" "q-17518" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "z=\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2.034\\,\\text{i}}"] ["math" "z=\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}"] ["math" "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{0.034\\,\\text{i}}"] ["math" "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2.034\\,\\text{i}}"] ["math" "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/state.json" "file_sha256" "276dc